{
  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "ProcureFlow Monorepo — New Joiner Tour",
  "description": "End-to-end orientation for a new maintainer: npm workspaces, the sole React frontend, dual-base API client, Zoho-pattern workspace shell, NestJS backend, seed tenants, and the local proxy. Follow steps in order.",
  "steps": [
    {
      "directory": "apps",
      "title": "1. Monorepo layout",
      "description": "Situation: apps/web (sole frontend), apps/backend (NestJS local-only), apps/functions (what ships to Catalyst), packages/shared. Mechanism: npm workspaces in root package.json fan out dev/build/db scripts. Implication: never create a second frontend — all UI work lands in apps/web. Gotcha: Procurement-Local/ (if present) is a derived copy, not source."
    },
    {
      "file": "package.json",
      "line": 5,
      "title": "2. Workspaces + scripts",
      "description": "Situation: workspaces list plus dev:web / dev:backend / build:web / db:seed scripts. Mechanism: `npm run dev --workspace=apps/web` targets one package; db:push/seed forward to the backend workspace. Implication: this is how you run web (:5173), backend (:3000), and seed demo tenants. Gotcha: `npm run dev` backgrounds both — the user runs his own servers, so check netstat before starting duplicates."
    },
    {
      "file": "catalyst.json",
      "line": 12,
      "title": "3. What actually deploys",
      "description": "Situation: client.source = apps/web/dist served at /app; functions targets procurement_api + procurement_signup_gate. Mechanism: only the built dist ships — backend/ is local-only unless the tech lead confirms otherwise. Implication: frontend edits are invisible on :5174 until you rebuild dist. Gotcha: a stale dist hash + cached browser bundle is the #1 'my change did nothing' cause — rebuild, restart proxy, hard-reload."
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/web/src/main.tsx",
      "line": 7,
      "title": "4. React entry — one Router only",
      "description": "Situation: createRoot mounts <App/> inside a single <BrowserRouter>. Mechanism: routing context comes from here and nowhere else. Implication: adding a second <BrowserRouter> in App.tsx throws silently and blanks the page. Gotcha: grep for BrowserRouter must show exactly one hit (this file) — see skill pitfall #5."
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/web/src/App.tsx",
      "line": 9,
      "title": "5. Route map",
      "description": "Situation: /, /signin, /signup, /workspace with nested procurement pages (requests, approvals, items, vendors, pr, rfq, po, receives, bills, payments). Mechanism: nested /workspace routes render through <Outlet/> in the Workspace shell. Implication: every new sidebar entry needs a matching Route here plus a titleFor case in Workspace, or it falls through to /. Gotcha: alias extra paths (e.g. /workspace/my-requests → RequestsPage) instead of duplicating components."
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/web/src/api.ts",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "6. Dual-base API client",
      "description": "Situation: LOCAL_BASE=/api/v1 (Nest :3000, where demo@procureflow.io lives) vs CATALYST_BASE=/server/procurement_api/api/v1. Mechanism: auth tries local first, falls back to Catalyst on network failure or Invalid credentials; procurement lists try Catalyst first, fall back locally only on network error. Implication: wiring a button to an endpoint that exists on only one side yields [] or 401 on the other. Gotcha: both vite.config.ts and local-proxy.js must proxy /api → :3000, or Vite dev 401s while dist works."
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/web/src/features/workspace/Workspace.tsx",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "7. Workspace shell",
      "description": "Situation: fixed TopBar above a flex row (sidebar + main), page-title header, scrollable <Outlet/>. Mechanism: shell mounts once per page load — mount-gated boot loader plays on sign-in/hard refresh, never on in-app navigation. Implication: shell owns shared tab state; content views take view/onViewChange props and render content only (one tab bar per hierarchy). Gotcha: pushing tab content into TopBar breaks the persistent-bar contract."
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/web/src/features/workspace/TopBar.tsx",
      "line": 8,
      "title": "8. TopBar + global search",
      "description": "Situation: dark h-12 bar (logo, refresh, Zoho-pill search, trial banner, org switcher, blue + Quick Create, bell, settings, avatar, app grid). Mechanism: SEARCH_MODULES covers all workspace routes; hover moves a blue pill, click navigates with ?q, and useQueryFilter filters lists client-side. Implication: new routes must be added to SEARCH_MODULES or global search can't reach them. Gotcha: use real logo assets in public/img — never hand-draw the P-mark."
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/web/src/features/workspace/WorkspaceSidebar.tsx",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "9. Sidebar — Zoho-refined",
      "description": "Situation: 220px/76px rail, grouped nav (Home / Requests+Approvals / Items+Vendors / Procurement+Payables / Budgets+Analytics), active blue pill. Mechanism: submenus stay mounted inside grid-rows 0fr↔1fr transitions (glide both ways); icons come from one ICON_SRC map to public/img/icon-*.png. Implication: screenshot-driven rounds change one delta at a time (scale/spacing/hover/grouping) then rebuild + grep dist. Gotcha: never conditionally mount submenus, never add a second right-side chevron, keep rows full-bleed."
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/backend/src/main.ts",
      "line": 4,
      "title": "10. Backend bootstrap",
      "description": "Situation: NestFactory bootstrap with CORS for :5173/:5174/:5175 plus global ValidationPipe. Mechanism: Prisma client connects eagerly on onModuleInit — no Postgres on :5432 means P1001 and the backend can't start at all. Implication: backend is read-only for frontend agents (supervisor owns it) — diagnose, don't edit. Gotcha: EPERM on prisma generate while backend holds the engine DLL → use --skip-generate, then regenerate + restart."
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/backend/src/app.module.ts",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "11. Backend module wiring",
      "description": "Situation: Prisma + Auth + Items/Vendors/PRs/POs/procurement controllers; WorkspaceController registered alongside HealthController. Mechanism: TenantPrismaService auto-scopes reads by tenantId, but the same hook breaks update({where:{id}}) — use updateMany + refetch for single-row writes. Implication: before building a UI button, grep backend src/<module>/ for the action — omit the button until the endpoint lands. Gotcha: duplicate GET /health on the same api/v1 prefix crashes routing — health lives only in HealthController."
    },
    {
      "file": "apps/backend/prisma/seed.ts",
      "line": 6,
      "title": "12. Seed tenants + demo login",
      "description": "Situation: seeds Acme/Globex tenants plus demo@procureflow.io / Demo123! (and demo@procureflow.local variants). Mechanism: `npx prisma db push` then `npm run db:seed` provisions login + real rows for items/vendors. Implication: smoke-test with the demo token; expect items/vendors rows, orders [] (stub until procurement flow lands), 401 without token. Gotcha: no delete endpoint — name smoke-test creates timestamped (QA Item <epoch>) and disclose leftovers."
    },
    {
      "file": "local-proxy.js",
      "line": 6,
      "title": "13. Local proxy :5174",
      "description": "Situation: serves apps/web/dist at root, proxies /api/* → localhost:3000 and /server/* + /__catalyst/* → live Catalyst. Mechanism: mirrors vite.config.ts server.proxy so dev (:5173, serves src) and proxy (:5174, serves dist) hit the same backends. Implication: after every frontend edit rebuild, confirm the new string is in dist/assets/*.js, restart the proxy so it picks up the new index.html hash, then Ctrl+Shift+R. Gotcha: strip the leading slash before path.join(WEB_DIR, …) — otherwise static files return 0 bytes and boot sticks on 'Connecting…'."
    },
    {
      "title": "Next Steps",
      "description": "You can now: sign in with demo@procureflow.io / Demo123!, trace a request from TopBar search → sidebar route → pages.tsx list → api.ts base → Nest controller → Prisma tenant scope, and run `npm run build` in apps/web plus the :3000/:5174 smoke curls to verify any change."
    }
  ]
}
